  "files": {},
  "metadata": {
    "title": "One multilingual model, many transfer paths",
    "description": "A multilingual model shares a vocabulary and Transformer weights across languages. Fine-tuning on English and testing on Hindi is zero-shot cross-lingual transfer. Shared subwords, structure, and representation geometry help; data imbalance and fixed capacity make transfer uneven, so sampling with n_i^alpha can up-weight smaller languages."
  }
